      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
          "content": "Serum monomeric immunoglobulin A (IgA) has powerful immunomodulatory roles in its ability to suppress immune responses. Monomeric IgA acts through FcalphaRI, which plays a significant role in vivo in maintaining the integrity of immune responses by an inhibitory immunoreceptor tyrosine-based activation motif-mediated process and powerful inhibitory cellular effector mechanisms elicited by the IgA system."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Triggering of FcalphaRI-mediated inhibitory function by Fab anti-FcalphaRI-mediated inhibitory function is able to inhibit several inflammatory and autoimmune diseases including asthma and glomerulonephritis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The use of monomeric IgA as a therapeutic tool in human inflammatory diseases may offer much potential."
        }
      ]},
